WEBVTT

00:00.700 --> 00:02.865
This is a live engine.

00:02.915 --> 00:05.626
Every point is a word it knows.

00:05.676 --> 00:09.180
Every line is a connection it has made for itself.

00:09.230 --> 00:14.230
Two research projects run on it: Neuron, and Cortex.

00:15.092 --> 00:16.645
Neuron.

00:16.695 --> 00:20.120
Ask it to define a word it has never been given.

00:20.726 --> 00:26.797
It reads its sources, and works the word into the graph, along with every word it met on the way.

00:26.847 --> 00:28.972
Twenty-nine runs.

00:29.022 --> 00:31.303
Thirteen new words.

00:31.353 --> 00:33.241
Two seconds.

00:33.851 --> 00:41.259
One typed line, and a tree of runs underneath it: the engine asking its own questions, and answering them.

00:42.851 --> 00:46.331
Ask the same thing again, and nothing runs.

00:46.381 --> 00:48.506
It already knows.

00:48.556 --> 00:52.165
Learning happens once, and takes its time.

00:52.215 --> 00:54.454
Recall is immediate.

00:55.060 --> 00:57.520
A meaning is not fixed.

01:00.269 --> 01:04.722
It can be told, and it can be changed, in a single line.

01:05.269 --> 01:09.465
Every run leaves a receipt: the path it took through the graph.

01:09.515 --> 01:13.213
Any run can be played back, hop by hop.

01:14.269 --> 01:15.939
Cortex.

01:15.989 --> 01:23.372
The same engine, holding a project: its scope, its checkpoints, what is expected, and where things stand.

01:25.269 --> 01:28.775
Each session reports what it did, as a line.

01:28.825 --> 01:32.760
Say a thing twice, and it is not stored twice.

01:32.810 --> 01:36.119
It is the same memory, with a new time.

01:36.169 --> 01:40.791
The next session starts from the state of the work, not from a transcript.

01:41.836 --> 01:43.988
Cortex and Neuron.

01:44.038 --> 01:47.569
Research and engineering by James Huson.

01:47.619 --> 01:50.522
Find both at exnulla dot com.
